/* ═══ AJOUT lot 6 anglais 3e (abonnés) (hors build principal : source à verser dans le dossier des sources) ═══ */
VRT_L("tle-a-anglais-reported-speech",{"titre":"Direct and indirect (reported) speech","duree":35,"famille":"Environment, well-being and health","agir":"Report what someone said, changing tenses, pronouns and time words correctly","accroche":"The weather man said: “It will rain tomorrow.” Two days later, you tell your friend: “He said it would rain the next day.” Why did “will” become “would” and “tomorrow” become “the next day”?","intro":"Ekwalla reports the weather forecast he heard on the radio in Limbe. His mistakes will show you the rules of reported speech.","objectifs":["distinguish direct and indirect speech","change tenses when the reporting verb is in the past (backshift)","change pronouns and time and place words","report questions and orders"],"enquete":{"titre":"The weather forecast in Limbe","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A radio on a table broadcasting the weather; a boy listens, then tells his grandmother on a veranda facing the sea' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='spC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#BFD9EA'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#spC)'/><rect y='150' width='640' height='70' fill='#4A7FA8'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#C9A06E'/><rect x='80' y='120' width='70' height='40' rx='6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='102' cy='140' r='10' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='120' y='130' width='22' height='4' fill='#F7C948'/><g transform='translate(230 100)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(420 100)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='40' y='40' width='220' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='150' y='60' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>“It will rain tomorrow.”</text><rect x='320' y='30' width='280' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='460' y='50' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>He said it would rain the next day.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Limbe, Ekwalla tells his grandmother what the radio said.","contexte":"<p>The radio said: “It will rain heavily tomorrow. Fishermen must stay on shore.” The next day, Ekwalla tells his grandmother: “The radio said it will rain heavily tomorrow and that fishermen must stay on shore.” His English teacher, who heard him, says: “Your message is right, but your grammar is not reported speech yet.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Two ways of reporting","html":"<p>Direct speech repeats the exact words between quotation marks. Indirect (reported) speech gives the meaning, without quotation marks, and adapts tenses, pronouns and time words.</p>"}],"question":"How do we change direct speech into indirect speech correctly?","tache":"Learn the backshift of tenses, the changes of pronouns and time words, then correct Ekwalla's report.","hypotheses":["In reported speech, we just remove the quotation marks.","We change only the pronouns, never the tenses.","When the reporting verb is in the past, tenses go one step back, and pronouns and time words change to fit the new situation."]},"parties":[{"t":"Direct and indirect speech","html":"<div class='def'><b>Direct speech</b>The exact words of a speaker, between quotation marks: <em>He said, “I am tired.”</em></div><div class='def'><b>Indirect (reported) speech</b>The words of a speaker reported without quotation marks, usually after <em>say</em> or <em>tell</em>, often with <em>that</em>: <em>He said (that) he was tired.</em></div><ul><li><strong>say</strong> + (that) : <em>She said that she was hungry.</em></li><li><strong>tell</strong> + person + (that) : <em>She told me that she was hungry.</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>reporting verb (said / told me) + that + reported clause</p><div class='ex'><b>Example</b>Direct: <em>Ngum said, “I like football.”</em> → Indirect: <em>Ngum said (that) she liked football.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>French speakers, watch out!</b><em>Say</em> has no person object: not « he said me » but <em>he told me</em> or <em>he said to me</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"From direct to indirect","legende":"Quotation marks disappear; a reporting verb and that introduce the reported clause.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 200' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: direct and indirect speech' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Two ways of reporting</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Direct</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>exact words</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>“quotation marks”</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He said, “I am…”</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Indirect</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>meaning</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>no quotation marks</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He said that he was…</text><text x='634' y='195' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Ekwalla removed the quotation marks, but he kept “will” and “tomorrow”. That is not enough: reported speech also changes <strong>tenses</strong> and <strong>time words</strong>.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Removing the quotation marks is not enough: tenses and time words change too."]]},"retenir":"Direct: exact words in quotes; indirect: say / tell + that, adapted words."},{"t":"Backshift: changing the tenses","verrou":true},{"t":"Pronouns, time words, questions and orders","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Time words in reported speech. When we report later, words that point to the moment of speaking must change.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 230' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: time words, place words and questions in reported speech' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='230' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='230' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Direct → reported</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='172' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Time</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>today → that day</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>tomorrow → the next day</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>yesterday → the day before</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>now → then</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='172' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Place</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>here → there</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>this → that</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>these → those</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='172' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Questions</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>“Are you…?” →</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>asked if I was</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>“Where…?” →</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>asked where I lived</text><text x='634' y='225' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Vers le Baccalauréat","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"Tle A","rang":41,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"CITIZENSHIP AND HUMAN RIGHTS","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about citizenship and human rights","situation":"The radio said: “It will rain heavily tomorrow. Fishermen must stay on shore.” The next day, Ekwalla tells his grandmother: “The radio said it will rain heavily tomorrow and that fishermen must stay on shore.” His English teacher, who heard him, says: “Your message is right, but your grammar is not reported speech yet.”","tache":"Learn the backshift of tenses, the changes of pronouns and time words, then correct Ekwalla's report."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("tle-a-anglais-passive-voice",{"titre":"Active and passive voices","duree":35,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Change sentences from the active to the passive voice and choose the voice that fits the message","accroche":"“Workers in Douala make chocolate.” “Chocolate is made in Douala.” Same fact, two voices. Why would a journalist choose the second?","intro":"Mbah writes an article for the school magazine about a cocoa factory in Douala. His sentences will help you master the passive voice.","objectifs":["recognise the active and the passive voice","form the passive (be + past participle) in the main tenses","use by + agent only when necessary","choose the voice according to what is important in the message"],"enquete":{"titre":"The school magazine article","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A factory hall with a conveyor belt carrying bags of cocoa beans that come out as chocolate bars; a student journalist takes notes' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='paC2' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3EAF4'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#paC2)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#8F8A80'/><rect x='120' y='130' width='400' height='14' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='150' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#8B5A2B'/><rect x='230' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#8B5A2B'/><rect x='360' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#4A2511'/><rect x='450' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#4A2511'/><rect x='290' y='70' width='50' height='60' fill='#C9CED6'/><g transform='translate(70 100)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1E499B'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1E499B'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#F4F1EA'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#F4F1EA' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#F4F1EA' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='86' y='126' width='20' height='26' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='260' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='150' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Chocolate is made here…</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Douala, Mbah visits a cocoa processing factory for the school magazine.","contexte":"<p>Mbah writes: “Somebody grows the cocoa in the South Region. Somebody makes the chocolate here. People have exported the chocolate to Nigeria by people.” His teacher comments: “Too many ‘somebody’! Use the passive voice, and don't write ‘by people’.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Two voices","html":"<p>In the active voice, the subject does the action. In the passive voice, the subject receives the action; the doer (agent) is introduced by <em>by</em> or left out.</p>"}],"question":"How do we form the passive voice, and when should we use it?","tache":"Form the passive in the main tenses, decide when to keep or remove the agent, then rewrite Mbah's article.","hypotheses":["The passive is just the active with by added at the end.","We must always mention the agent with by.","The passive is be (in the tense of the active verb) + past participle; we use it when the action matters more than the doer, and we drop the agent when it is unknown or obvious."]},"parties":[{"t":"Active and passive voices","html":"<div class='def'><b>Active voice</b>The subject does the action: <em><u>Workers</u> make chocolate.</em></div><div class='def'><b>Passive voice</b>The subject receives the action: <em><u>Chocolate</u> is made (by workers).</em> The object of the active sentence becomes the subject of the passive sentence.</div><p class='formule'>passive = be (same tense as the active verb) + past participle (+ by + agent)</p><div class='ex'><b>Example</b>Active: <em>Farmers grow cocoa in the South Region.</em> → Passive: <em>Cocoa is grown in the South Region (by farmers).</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Watch out!</b>Only verbs with an object can become passive: « The bus arrived » has no passive.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"From active to passive","legende":"The object moves to the front, the verb becomes be + past participle, and the subject becomes the agent (by…), often dropped.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: active and passive sentence' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Active → passive</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Active</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Workers</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>make</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>chocolate.</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ subject acts</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Passive</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Chocolate</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>is made</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>(by workers).</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ subject receives</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Somebody grows the cocoa” tells us nothing about the doer: the important thing is the cocoa. The passive puts it first: “The cocoa <strong>is grown</strong> in the South Region.”</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","The passive is not just “by” added: the object becomes the subject and the verb becomes be + past participle."]]},"retenir":"Passive: object → subject; be + past participle; by + agent."},{"t":"The passive in the main tenses","verrou":true},{"t":"When to use the passive and the agent","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Baccalauréat","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"Tle A","rang":60,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"MEDIA AND COMMUNICATION","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about media and communication","situation":"Mbah writes: “Somebody grows the cocoa in the South Region. Somebody makes the chocolate here. People have exported the chocolate to Nigeria by people.” His teacher comments: “Too many ‘somebody’! Use the passive voice, and don't write ‘by people’.”","tache":"Form the passive in the main tenses, decide when to keep or remove the agent, then rewrite Mbah's article."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
/* ═══ FIN lot 6 anglais 3e (abonnés) ═══ */
